# data-validation-flow

The data validation pipeline implements critical geological and well data processing rules:

## Well Data Validation Workflow
Importance Score: 92/100

1. Depth Validation
- Enforces monotonically increasing depth curves
- Validates against geological formation constraints
- Preserves geological features during signal processing
- Classifies data gaps using domain thresholds

2. Gap Classification System
- 200-point threshold (~100m at 0.5m spacing) distinguishes:
  - Geological features (cased holes, non-logging zones)
  - Data errors (tool/transmission failures)
- Classification determines preservation vs interpolation strategy

3. Unit Conversion Rules
- Specialized handling of impedance values (thousands range)
- Geological-context validation for porosity percentages
- Domain-specific conversion validation requirements

## Well Information Processing
Importance Score: 85/100

1. Mandatory Field Validation
- Well name
- UWI (Unique Well Identifier)
- Field designation
- Operating company
- Valid depth range

2. Geological Quality Assessment
- Gap metrics based on formation context
- Shape mismatch detection for geological validity
- Formation-specific validation rules

3. LAS Header Processing
- Industry-standard header validation
- Depth range geological reasonableness checks
- Well identification cross-validation

